WEBVTT

00:01.320 --> 00:04.400
Hey, Squishy!

00:01.950 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:04.400 --> 00:07.440
Where are you? Answer me!

00:12.810 --> 00:13.400
Squishy?

00:15.120 --> 00:16.780
Satoshi... Serena...

00:17.240 --> 00:17.980
Did you find it?

00:18.480 --> 00:19.100
No.

00:19.760 --> 00:21.350
Seriously, where has it gone?

00:24.720 --> 00:25.630
Squishy...

00:30.370 --> 00:36.040
Eureka and Squishy!

00:46.740 --> 00:47.300
Eureka?

00:48.590 --> 00:49.730
Make sure to eat well.

00:50.060 --> 00:59.940
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

00:50.060 --> 00:59.940
Z

00:50.190 --> 00:52.350
You need energy to be able to look for Squishy.

00:56.080 --> 00:56.880
Thanks.

00:57.550 --> 00:59.280
I wonder what Squishy is doing.

00:59.680 --> 01:00.980
I wonder if it has recovered...

01:01.390 --> 01:03.300
I am sure it has. Do not worry.

01:03.970 --> 01:05.410
That is why you need to eat too, Eureka.

01:05.760 --> 01:07.100
He's right, Eureka.

01:07.710 --> 01:08.510
Yeah...

01:14.460 --> 01:14.880
Cell?

01:15.330 --> 01:15.890
So many?

01:18.130 --> 01:18.830
"Cell"...

01:19.040 --> 01:20.110
What is it, Citron?

01:21.010 --> 01:21.420
It is just...

01:21.890 --> 01:22.720
"Cell"...

01:23.340 --> 01:26.260
That is what those people who are after Squishy said.

01:27.120 --> 01:29.970
It is true that Squishy has some mysterious power.

01:30.500 --> 01:32.210
I guess you could say...

01:33.150 --> 01:34.230
...it is an extremely rare Pokémon.

01:35.150 --> 01:35.780
That's why...

01:36.820 --> 01:39.560
That's why it's getting targeted by those bad people.

01:41.040 --> 01:42.270
They're probably still chasing after it!

01:42.750 --> 01:45.340
They might have captured it and started doing horrible things to it already!

01:45.820 --> 01:48.280
We have to go save it! Squishy's in danger!

01:48.780 --> 01:49.560
Eureka...

01:49.560 --> 01:50.320
Calm down!

01:50.800 --> 01:52.930
Aren't you worried, bro?

01:52.930 --> 01:54.270
Of course I am!

01:54.720 --> 01:57.330
But it would be dangerous to go look for it at this hour!

01:57.740 --> 02:01.040
Squishy might be in much more danger!

02:01.040 --> 02:02.210
Wait, Eureka!

02:02.530 --> 02:03.730
Let go!

02:03.730 --> 02:05.260
Listen to your brother!

02:05.710 --> 02:06.460
But...!

02:06.690 --> 02:07.720
But Squishy...!

02:08.140 --> 02:11.180
This is not just about Squishy! If you were to disappear as well, Eureka...!

02:19.630 --> 02:20.410
Eureka...

02:21.060 --> 02:21.980
But...

02:22.860 --> 02:28.740
But I promised Squishy that I'd protect it no matter what, and that I wouldn't let it go...

02:30.160 --> 02:32.530
I know. We will find it tomorrow for sure.

02:33.060 --> 02:34.080
Leave it to your brother.

02:37.300 --> 02:37.590
Okay.

02:39.060 --> 02:42.620
All right, let's watch our faces and go to bed for tonight. Okay?

02:43.630 --> 02:44.310
Yeah...

03:03.250 --> 03:03.920
She's sleeping.

03:04.660 --> 03:06.780
Thank you, Serena.

03:07.230 --> 03:10.060
But it's no wonder that Eureka is worried.

03:10.640 --> 03:12.350
Who are those people?

03:12.830 --> 03:14.990
I wonder what they're trying to achieve by capturing Squishy.

03:16.060 --> 03:18.200
Things are just getting more and more mysterious.

03:18.900 --> 03:22.250
If Squishy ran away from us...

03:22.830 --> 03:25.840
Even if that is the case, I want to give her the chance to say goodbye properly.

03:27.060 --> 03:29.380
We have to find it. For Eureka's sake as well....

03:29.870 --> 03:31.040
Yeah, of course.

03:31.520 --> 03:34.260
After all, Squishy is Eureka's... <i>our</i> friend.

03:34.850 --> 03:36.270
Let's try our best again tomorrow!

03:36.820 --> 03:37.260
Yes.

03:39.540 --> 03:41.480
This is the pursuit squad's periodic call.

03:42.300 --> 03:45.240
Those Trainers still haven't met up with Z1.

03:46.160 --> 03:47.600
Continue keeping them under constant watch.

03:48.110 --> 03:48.660
Understood.

03:49.680 --> 03:50.690
Any reactions from the sensors?

03:51.310 --> 03:55.130
None. Z1's current location is still unknown.

03:56.400 --> 03:59.200
Oh my, it really likes hide-and-seek.

03:59.790 --> 04:01.250
It's time we find it.

04:01.890 --> 04:03.550
Expand the radius of the sensors!

04:04.030 --> 04:04.290
Understood!

04:08.210 --> 04:10.350
All right, Eureka. Let's set off!

04:11.840 --> 04:12.820
Let's go, Dedenne!

04:14.850 --> 04:15.710
Please wait.

04:16.320 --> 04:18.060
Leave this to me.

04:18.860 --> 04:20.220
By "leave it to me", do you mean...?

04:20.640 --> 04:22.260
Heh heh heh heh....

04:22.640 --> 04:25.150
Now it is time for science to open up the future!

04:25.680 --> 04:27.400
Citronic Gear, on!

04:28.020 --> 04:30.530
This is the perfect machine for searching Squishy!

04:30.960 --> 04:33.820
I call it "I'll Find Squishy For Sure Mark I"!

04:34.400 --> 04:35.890
Bro, I expect great things!

04:35.890 --> 04:37.620
This is the power of technology!

04:37.950 --> 04:44.210
This is an exceptional machine that automatically finds the kind of sunny spots that Squishy likes.

04:44.900 --> 04:46.920
Citron, when did you build that?

04:47.780 --> 04:51.670
Secretly building things for the sake of one's cute sister is what makes an inventor.

04:52.480 --> 04:53.490
Bro...

04:55.040 --> 04:58.130
All right, go,  I'll Find Squishy For Sure Mark I!

04:58.400 --> 05:00.310
Find Squishy for sure!

05:03.540 --> 05:04.700
Has it found it already?

05:05.020 --> 05:06.820
All right, let's follow, everyone!

05:10.540 --> 05:13.980
I can't believe Squishy had so much power.

05:13.980 --> 05:17.200
If we get that thing, there's no doubt our offensive capabilities will increase.

05:17.710 --> 05:19.780
Conquering the world will become a piece of cake, too.

05:20.030 --> 05:22.690
What's getting in the way is that glasses gang that pretends to be cool.

05:23.140 --> 05:25.440
That bunch seems to be strong.

05:25.440 --> 05:30.830
Well, let's take a long rest to restore our energy in preparation for our fight against them, then!

05:39.090 --> 05:39.970
What's that?

05:44.980 --> 05:46.190
Whoa, what's this?!

05:53.180 --> 05:55.240
Aw, geez! You're so annoying!

06:03.680 --> 06:05.650
I have a hunch this isn't going to end well!

06:05.890 --> 06:08.690
Our hunches are never wrong in times like this!

06:09.020 --> 06:10.000
He that fights and runs away may live to fight another day!

06:16.770 --> 06:19.230
I wonder where your machine went, bro.

06:20.740 --> 06:24.180
No worries! I made sure to attach a tracking device.

06:30.500 --> 06:32.860
Ah, my masterpiece!

06:35.630 --> 06:36.480
Dokurog?

06:39.310 --> 06:42.910
Dokurog, the Poison Jab Pokémon. The evolved form of Gureggru.

06:43.300 --> 06:49.120
It has a poison sac at its throat. When it croaks, the stored poison is churned for greater potency.

06:50.590 --> 06:52.140
They look kinda angry.

06:52.140 --> 06:55.550
Is it possible that the machine did something to the Dokurog...?

06:55.550 --> 06:57.120
Is that why they look so tattered?

06:57.120 --> 06:58.130
That must be it.

07:00.420 --> 07:02.000
Horubee, Mud Shot!

07:07.470 --> 07:08.190
Now is our chance!

07:10.500 --> 07:12.590
We are not your enemies!

07:12.590 --> 07:13.710
Please stop, Dokurog!

07:23.820 --> 07:25.310
Eipam Arm, activate!

07:29.780 --> 07:30.790
Eureka!

07:31.500 --> 07:32.000
Horubee!

07:43.120 --> 07:43.780
Eureka!

07:44.140 --> 07:44.760
Are you all right?

07:46.800 --> 07:48.300
I'm fine.

07:49.420 --> 07:50.780
Thank goodness.

07:59.980 --> 08:00.580
Horubee?

08:01.010 --> 08:02.130
Show me, please.

08:06.480 --> 08:07.370
This is...

08:08.030 --> 08:09.470
Horubee, are you okay?

08:09.840 --> 08:11.120
You have to get treated quickly.

08:11.120 --> 08:12.210
To the Pokémon Center!

08:14.900 --> 08:16.460
Please hold on, Horubee.

08:19.060 --> 08:22.740
So the brats still haven't met up with Squishy.

08:23.150 --> 08:26.860
If we tail them, we might be able to meet Squishy.

08:27.230 --> 08:29.460
If we don't, we'll just take Pikachu.

08:29.900 --> 08:31.540
Let's get started right away.

08:38.240 --> 08:40.030
We have caught energy waves coming from Z2.

08:40.880 --> 08:43.870
Z1 appears to be responding, but it's outside the radius of the sensors.

08:44.850 --> 08:50.240
Oh my. What are Z1 and Z2 whispering about?

08:51.010 --> 08:53.870
Adjust the sensors. Calculate Z1's location.

08:54.210 --> 08:54.620
Understood!

09:00.620 --> 09:03.170
Danger increasing further.

09:03.620 --> 09:04.350
Caution.

09:05.540 --> 09:09.220
Cut contact with humans completely.

09:09.660 --> 09:11.200
That is at odds with the truth.

09:12.030 --> 09:15.730
We want to observe these entities called humans...

09:16.560 --> 09:18.100
Cannot approve.

09:18.900 --> 09:21.620
Humans disrupt order.

09:22.320 --> 09:26.900
Destroyers progressing with the breakdown of Kalos.

09:26.900 --> 09:29.550
We will not arrive at a shared perception of this matter.

09:30.270 --> 09:31.970
We will reserve our answer.

09:48.560 --> 09:49.650
Pokémon Quiz!

09:50.030 --> 09:51.100
The answer is...?

10:02.370 --> 10:04.880
Joy-san, will Horubee get better?

10:05.390 --> 10:05.980
Of course.

10:06.750 --> 10:07.230
But...

10:08.260 --> 10:09.920
...we're out of Kidamo...

10:11.550 --> 10:12.300
"Kidamo"?

10:15.100 --> 10:15.910
Do you mean this?

10:16.750 --> 10:17.890
That's right. It's a medicinal plant.

10:18.380 --> 10:21.840
There are some growing near the top of the mountain out back, so I'll go  pick them real quick.

10:22.590 --> 10:23.260
Excuse me.

10:24.050 --> 10:25.260
Joy-san, please come.

10:25.630 --> 10:26.670
Okay, I'll be right there.

10:27.180 --> 10:28.700
I'm sorry. Please wait a second.

10:44.340 --> 10:45.570
We didn't make it in time, huh...?

10:47.300 --> 10:49.110
Give me Z1's current location.

10:49.970 --> 10:52.660
It stopped emitting energy waves, so we've lost sight of it.

10:53.260 --> 10:54.700
Geez... Useless.

10:55.970 --> 10:57.730
This is Bara. Can you hear me?

10:58.420 --> 11:00.100
Yes, this is the pursuit squad.

11:00.850 --> 11:02.080
Where are those Trainers?

11:02.610 --> 11:05.470
Right now, they're all staying at the Pokémon Center.

11:06.300 --> 11:10.340
One of their Pokémon has taken damage, so they are now preoccupied by that.

11:10.980 --> 11:11.490
Understood.

11:12.500 --> 11:14.770
They can't seem to be bothered about Z1 at the moment.

11:15.810 --> 11:19.570
Maybe it abandoned them because it suspected we're watching them.

11:20.140 --> 11:22.350
In that case it wouldn't just nonchalantly go back to them.

11:24.580 --> 11:25.890
Pursuit squad, withdraw.

11:26.780 --> 11:29.630
We'll narrow our search for Z1 down to Area R.

11:35.920 --> 11:36.620
Where is Eureka?

11:38.050 --> 11:39.840
She was there just a moment ago.

11:45.040 --> 11:45.880
It cannot be...!

11:46.460 --> 11:51.420
All right... All right... All right...

11:52.400 --> 11:54.460
We've got to help Horubee...

11:55.100 --> 11:55.650
Quick...

11:56.660 --> 12:00.880
It's only because I was so selfish to everyone that Horubee got...

12:07.380 --> 12:09.410
Yeah, we have to be careful.

12:19.630 --> 12:21.170
We've made it through the first obstacle.

12:26.960 --> 12:27.390
All right.

12:27.980 --> 12:28.480
Let's go!

12:39.840 --> 12:44.340
Please let us through! We have to get to the top!

13:05.010 --> 13:05.930
Everyone!

13:06.750 --> 13:07.470
Are you all right?

13:07.840 --> 13:08.500
Bro!

13:17.200 --> 13:19.390
Pikachu, Tairenar, good job!

13:21.730 --> 13:24.480
Why did you come on your own? We were worried!

13:25.070 --> 13:26.430
But Horubee...

13:27.020 --> 13:29.900
It's my fault that Horubee...

13:31.540 --> 13:32.900
Your fault?

13:35.360 --> 13:40.030
No. Horubee wanted to support you in your desperate search for Squishy!

13:40.430 --> 13:41.580
But... But...

13:42.320 --> 13:43.120
Do you not understand?

13:43.730 --> 13:47.140
We cherish Squishy as much as you do, Eureka.

13:48.480 --> 13:49.310
Did you not think so?

13:50.060 --> 13:53.340
Squishy is a friend to <i>all</i> of us.

13:55.150 --> 13:56.140
Bro...

13:57.310 --> 13:59.630
It's just as Citron says, Eureka.

14:03.180 --> 14:04.060
Everyone...

14:06.100 --> 14:07.950
All right, the medicinal plant comes first.

14:08.370 --> 14:10.810
Let's find it quickly and help Horubee get better!

14:11.180 --> 14:11.620
Yeah.

14:12.030 --> 14:12.420
Yes.

14:12.820 --> 14:13.540
Let's go, let's go!

14:17.440 --> 14:17.860
Pikachu!

14:20.980 --> 14:22.960
If you ask "Pikachu?",

14:23.380 --> 14:25.410
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

14:26.060 --> 14:27.910
To prevent the world's destruction!

14:28.580 --> 14:30.820
To protect the world's peace!

14:30.820 --> 14:33.330
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

14:33.820 --> 14:36.420
we're lovely, charmy villains!

14:37.440 --> 14:38.000
Musashi!

14:38.460 --> 14:38.970
Kojiro!

14:39.760 --> 14:42.510
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

14:42.770 --> 14:45.550
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

14:45.550 --> 14:47.070
Just kidding!

14:50.590 --> 14:51.580
Rocket Gang!

14:52.380 --> 14:54.960
As usual, we're taking Pikachu!

14:54.960 --> 14:58.850
We never let go of prey we've set our eyes on. That's how we roll.

14:58.850 --> 15:00.510
Now then, everyone, bye!

15:03.390 --> 15:04.500
Leave this to us.

15:04.750 --> 15:06.500
Citron, Eureka, you two go!

15:07.490 --> 15:08.560
Get the medicinal plant for Horubee!

15:08.910 --> 15:09.460
Quick!

15:10.160 --> 15:10.960
Understood.

15:11.600 --> 15:12.060
Eureka.

15:12.740 --> 15:13.170
Yeah.

15:16.770 --> 15:17.950
Come out, Gekkouga!

15:19.090 --> 15:20.640
Gekkouga, Water Shuriken!

15:20.640 --> 15:21.970
Tairenar, Flamethrower!

15:30.160 --> 15:32.400
That's an early crash!

15:36.900 --> 15:37.780
Pikachu!

15:38.640 --> 15:39.890
Welcome back, Pikachu!

15:41.090 --> 15:42.930
Argh! Go, Pumpjin!

15:42.930 --> 15:44.200
I'll count on you, Maaiika!

15:49.060 --> 15:49.950
Let's go, everyone!

15:50.450 --> 15:50.720
Yeah!

15:55.300 --> 15:56.740
This seems to be the top.

15:57.090 --> 15:57.770
And the Kidamo?

15:58.160 --> 15:59.970
Uh... Uh...

16:00.290 --> 16:01.260
Ah, bro!

16:02.180 --> 16:02.660
Over there!

16:08.990 --> 16:09.890
Whoa...

16:10.690 --> 16:11.340
There it is!

16:11.790 --> 16:13.460
That is Kidamo, Eureka!

16:13.940 --> 16:14.940
All right!

16:16.270 --> 16:18.320
Now Horubee can get better!

16:18.620 --> 16:20.360
Yeah. Let us get it quickly and go back!

16:29.310 --> 16:31.280
Maaiika, Psybeam!

16:31.280 --> 16:32.830
Pumpjin, Dark Pulse!

16:35.920 --> 16:37.550
Pikachu, Iron Tail!

16:38.110 --> 16:39.880
Gekkouga, Aerial Ace!

16:40.340 --> 16:41.740
Tairenar, Scratch!

16:49.330 --> 16:50.990
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

16:51.250 --> 16:52.600
Gekkouga, Water Shuriken!

16:52.960 --> 16:54.480
Tairenar, Fire Blast!

17:04.540 --> 17:06.850
This feels bad!

17:10.580 --> 17:11.230
All right!

17:12.110 --> 17:13.520
Well done, Pikachu, Gekkouga.

17:14.940 --> 17:17.360
All right, let's follow Citron and Eureka.

17:17.730 --> 17:18.080
Yeah.

17:24.320 --> 17:26.270
We have to help Horubee get better.

17:26.670 --> 17:27.760
Do your best, Dedenne!

17:47.500 --> 17:48.880
Dedenne, try once more!

18:08.050 --> 18:09.140
All right!

18:09.630 --> 18:11.170
Eureka, Dedenne!

18:14.830 --> 18:16.100
Thank you, bro!

18:16.400 --> 18:17.600
You are welcome.

18:17.980 --> 18:19.540
Citron! Eureka!

18:20.260 --> 18:21.490
We found it!

18:24.400 --> 18:25.650
Well done, Eureka!

18:25.910 --> 18:27.730
Now Horubee will get better!

18:28.060 --> 18:28.540
Yeah.

18:29.550 --> 18:31.040
Just wait, Horubee.

18:42.240 --> 18:44.880
Thanks for waiting. It has recovered.

18:46.030 --> 18:46.800
Horubee!

18:47.140 --> 18:48.380
I was worried!

18:49.330 --> 18:51.760
I'm so glad for you, bro, Horubee.

18:52.210 --> 18:53.600
Thank you, Eureka.

18:55.010 --> 18:57.680
No, bro, it's all thanks to you guys.

18:58.130 --> 18:59.500
I'm the one who has to say thank you.

19:01.550 --> 19:06.320
All right, now that Horubee has recovered, let's go search for Squishy again.

19:06.830 --> 19:07.260
Yeah.

19:06.830 --> 19:07.260
Yes.

19:07.680 --> 19:08.320
Let's go.

19:14.850 --> 19:16.240
Sunbathing is the key.

19:16.240 --> 19:17.790
A sunny place...

19:17.040 --> 19:18.750
What's the matter, Dedenne?

19:17.790 --> 19:19.330
Let's start searching there.

19:30.130 --> 19:30.840
Squishy!

19:31.170 --> 19:31.870
What?

19:31.870 --> 19:32.430
No way!

19:32.690 --> 19:36.060
Geez! I was so worried, Squishy!

19:37.620 --> 19:38.660
When did it...?

19:39.250 --> 19:42.400
Squishy must've been looking for you too, Eureka.

19:43.250 --> 19:44.110
You're right.

19:44.610 --> 19:48.190
You'll travel with us again, right?

19:51.420 --> 19:53.760
Thank you, Squishy!

19:53.760 --> 19:55.230
I'm so glad for you, Eureka.

19:55.230 --> 19:58.880
Yeah, now I won't let you go any more! We'll be together forever, promise!

20:01.950 --> 20:04.610
Squishy has safely returned to Eureka's side.

20:05.410 --> 20:06.400
What is Squishy...

20:07.260 --> 20:10.160
...and what are its intentions?

20:11.040 --> 20:12.090
Satoshi and his friends' journey is...

20:16.020 --> 20:21.010
Pokémon no Uchi Atsumaru?

20:16.020 --> 20:21.010
Sunday January 17th at 8am!

20:16.560 --> 20:21.010
Mega Abatalis!?

20:16.860 --> 20:18.690
Pokénchi on Sunday at 8 AM will be...

20:18.690 --> 20:19.540
...fluffy?!

20:19.860 --> 20:21.010
It's sweet!

20:19.900 --> 20:20.530
It's sweet!

20:24.110 --> 20:25.550
I love Horubee!

20:26.300 --> 20:29.570
This is a program about Horubee lovers for Horubee lovers brought to you by Horubee lovers:

20:29.570 --> 20:30.930
"I love Horubee!"

20:30.930 --> 20:33.060
I've discovered a lovely Horubee!

20:33.970 --> 20:36.510
This Horubee belongs to a Trainer from Miare City.

20:36.510 --> 20:37.970
Its ears that can dig through hard soil and...

20:37.970 --> 20:40.140
...the shape of its whiskers are the greatest!

20:41.260 --> 20:47.890
With the way this Horubee stops fights between Pokémon and expresses concern about them, it seems to fulfill a big brother role for everyone.

20:47.890 --> 20:49.520
So kind!

20:49.520 --> 20:52.400
It also helps out its Trainer like this!

20:52.400 --> 20:53.940
So faithful!

20:53.940 --> 20:56.480
We gotta keep watching this Horubee!

20:56.480 --> 20:57.500
Yeah!

20:58.530 --> 20:59.950
Horubee's funny faces!

21:02.980 --> 21:05.140
Who is it imitating?

21:07.200 --> 21:08.020
The correct answer is...

21:09.140 --> 21:10.980
Nyaonix!

21:11.180 --> 21:12.100
Did you get the answer?

21:12.350 --> 21:14.510
Now then, see you next Horubee!

21:18.210 --> 21:20.140
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:20.320 --> 21:21.380
Towards our next adventure!

21:22.450 --> 21:23.910
We were taking a break when...

21:24.300 --> 21:25.920
...we heard Onbat's voice echoing in the distance.

